<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115413" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψέλιον</span></b> , later sts. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψέλλιον</span></b>  (v. l. in
		<i><span class="en">
			X.
			<u>Cyr.</u>
			1.3.2
		</span></i>, never in <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
		</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
			<u>POsl.</u>
			46.8
		</span></i>
		<span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>Supp.Epigr.</u>
			7.428
		</span></i> (Dura, <span class="entity">iii A. D.</span>), in Inscrr. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψίλιον</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψίλλιον</span></b>  (qq. v.), τό:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>armlet</i> or <i>anklet,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψέλιον περὶ ἑκατέρῃ τῶν κνημέων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					4.168
				</span></i>
			; mostly in pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψέλια,</span> a
			favourite ornament of the Persians, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				3.20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				9.80
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				1.2.27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.3.2
			</span></i>; worn by women in Egypt, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				1101.8
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B. C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				259.11
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A. D.)</span>, etc., and in Greece, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.142c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> an iron
			implement, perh. agricultural, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				782
			</span></i> (<i>a</i>).<i><span class="en">
				42
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψελίου καὶ δρεπάνου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PPetr.</u>
					2p.113
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ Δωριεῖς</span>
		</div>
